{
    "background_story": "Lucy was a feisty and charismatic chef who owned a quaint deli in the heart of the city. She was particularly famous for her signature sandwich, 'Lucy's Zinger,' which featured a generous helping of her homemade horseradish sauce. The sauce was a family secret, passed down from her grandmother, and its pungent flavor added a kick that kept customers coming back for more. Lucy's passion for horseradish wasn't just about the flavor; it was also about the memories it evoked of her grandmother's kitchen, where she spent countless hours learning the art of cooking. As her deli's popularity grew, so did Lucy's reputation as a master of bold flavors and hearty portions, with her horseradish sauce remaining the crown jewel of her culinary creations.",
